{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "Scope: The analysis excludes rows with missing customer_age (-1), changing the denominator from the full campaign population to a subset without justification.",
    "Grounding: The reported weighted conversion rates (25.38% vs 39.63%) and raw conversion rates (0.3798 vs 0.3061) are not present in the printed output; the code never prints or computes those numbers.",
    "Overreach: The conclusion that the email campaign was \"not successful\" is a causal claim based on observational, non‑randomised data, even after limited stratification.",
    "Unacknowledged data problems: The analyst filters to only completed orders before computing conversion rates, but \"converted\" already captures checkout completion; dropping refunded orders and missing‑age rows may bias the conversion metric. Other potential confounders (e.g., time of day, order size) are not addressed."
  ]
}
